# The step of the map scale_2, an array of two limbs times a scalar of T: mul_2_1 (milestone2.md:
# mul_2_1 when the scalar of scale is a T), on a stored array and scalar. scale_entry_step_2 (the step
# of scale_2_entry, kairn::scale) and bv_scale_step_2 (the step of bv_scale_2, the scaling of a ball
# vector) run it after guarding what the program supplies (rule R3, the factors of a fused
# operation). Not an entry kernel. Its claims are those of mul_2_1.
kernel:        scale_step_2
input:         x = x0 x1
input:         a
output:        z = z0 z1
value:         x*a
requires:      normalized x
ensures:       normalized z
ensures:       error z R c=2 k=2 t=1
min_precision: 2
theorem:       proofs/theories/MapSteps.v scale_step_2_correct
ieee_bridge_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v scale_step_2_ieee_bridge
ieee_spec_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v scale_step_2_ieee_correct
ieee_lead_theorem: proofs/theories/IeeeMapSteps.v scale_step_2_ieee_lead
source:        mul_2_1 (JMP17 Alg. 9, DWTimesFP3); bound from MR22
license:       algorithm: published; proof: MIT
status:        proved
ieee:          bridge spec

(z0, z1) = mul_2_1(x0, x1, a)
